I was playing an orcish wizard in Spork and found myself on the Quest
Home level at a measly XP=12 with 125 hp  ... :)  So, I thought I'd
give the new Quest Leader changes a try.  I killed off the apprentices
one by one without much todo and then zapped Neferet with a magic
missile.  He responded with an aggressive series of Summon Nasties
that included: an ettin, a minotaur, an Olog-Hai, a master mind
flayer, a baluchitherium, a purple worm, and a Jabberwock.  A scroll
of scare monster gave me a couple of steps and then a scroll of earth
let me heal up after the initial beating.

I set myself up in the upper room off of the western corridor from the
throne room.  In the hallway below the door was a scroll of scare
monster.  I moved one square above the door and read a scroll of
earth.  Well, then Neferet walked through or over the boulder onto the
doorway and was slain with 3 or 4 magic missiles.  Then a knife (that
he had picked up) was shown on the square over the boulder and
suddenly I could see the hallway beyond the boulder as though the
boulder wasn't there.  Then the Olog-Hai and the master mind flayer
entered the hallway but did not move onto the square of the door so I
thought that the boulder must still be there because they were willing
to be killed while not moving next to me as Neferet had done.  But
then the minotaur moved next to me and I zapped him and unfortunately
myself, too, with sleep.  He killed me before I woke.

So, here are my questions:
Was the boulder south of me destroyed when Neferet moved onto it, or
did he "squeeze"?
Is it possible to see past a boulder if something dies and drops its
inventory on it?
Was the minotaur able to step onto the boulder, since it's an H?  And
is this true in Vanilla?

